		{
			"id": "eiMqhL-2lWIqnY7X2",
			"description": "Inferno Pistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A pistol-format melta weapon carried by Astartes command squads, Inquisitors and Tempestus officers wanting a point-blank answer to armour without a full meltagun's bulk; background consistently frames it as devastating at arm's length and near-useless at any real distance.\n\nDesign: Scaled down two dice from the meltagun anchor (8dx6(10) burn) to 6dx6(10) burn for a pistol- sized fuel cell, on a very short 5/25 range band matching the anchor's \"vehicle-killer at short range, much less beyond\" description. At short range 6dx6 averages 126, which - like the full meltagun - penetrates every AV10-14 row and any personal armour outright (effective DR under the (10) divisor never exceeds 44, even against AV14's DR 440); only the DR 1350 glacis of a Leman Russ front or Land Raider (eff. 135) holds, letting it through 36%. See the Meltagun entry for the beyond-½D check; the pistol's beyond-½D line is one die lower than the meltagun's (3d vs 4d), the same one-die-down relationship. Handling: min ST 9 (√(10×6)≈7.7, bumped for the bulky coil and reservoir a fusion weapon needs even at pistol scale, the same treatment the Plasma Pistol gets). RoF 1 at both range bands: melta weapons must vent and recharge between shots per framework.md, unlike the semi-automatic pistol families. Shots 3(5), Bulk -2 and Rcl 1 are ordinary pistol figures.",
