		{
			"id": "ePPyb3rkLMNLYLZOq",
			"description": "Meltagun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Imperium's dedicated close-range anti-armour infantry weapon, flash-vaporising the target's outer surface with a superheated fusion reaction; fiction across every era treats it as able to gut a tank at point-blank range and as nearly worthless at any distance, in sharp contrast to a lascannon's much longer reach.\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed melta anchor: 8dx6(10) burn at ½D, \"much less beyond\" 4dx6(3). Checked against the vehicle armour table with the exact dice distribution: AV14 (DR 440) has effective DR 44 against the (10) armour divisor; 8dx6 averages 168, always penetrating, and the same holds at every lower AV on the table. The DR 1350 glacis (a Leman Russ front or any face of a Land Raider) is effective DR 135, which it still beats 87% of the time at ½D range. The sharp drop-off is modelled as a second weapon line rather than a formula: beyond ½D the round keeps only half its dice (4d instead of 8d, the usual GURPS halving for range) but keeps a x6 multiplier and a much weaker (3) armour divisor instead of (10), representing the fusion reaction losing coherence and cohesion in open air before it reaches the target. Checked against the AV table: beyond ½D it averages 84, penetrating AV10 (DR 125, effective DR 41) 99% and AV11 (DR 185) 84% of the time, but only 56% against AV12 (DR 250, effective DR 83), 10% against AV13 (DR 340) and never against AV14 (DR 440) or the DR 1350 glacis - it does not beat the heaviest tanks beyond ½D. A very short 10/50 range band (versus a boltgun's 200/1000) captures the weapon's role as a close-assault specialist, not a rifle. Handling: min ST 13 (√(10×17)≈13.04, matching framework.md's sqrt formula almost exactly). RoF 1 (melta weapons must vent and recharge between shots). Bulk -4 and Rcl 1. Shared pattern: Astartes carry this same weapon (Deathwatch shows the same guns), so it is one stat block, not a human/Astartes split.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
