		{
			"id": "e64ziIFBU5EcDC7Nz",
			"description": "Multi-Melta",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A tripod- or vehicle-mounted heavy melta weapon fielded by heavy weapon teams and as a common tank sponson/hull weapon; background treats it exactly as a bigger meltagun, killing the heaviest vehicles at short range and rapidly losing effect beyond it.\n\nDesign: Two dice over the meltagun anchor (10dx6(10) vs 8dx6(10) short, 5dx6(3) vs 4dx6(3) beyond), matching this project's standard heavy-weapon progression, on a slightly longer 15/75 range band appropriate to a crew-served weapon with a bigger reactor. At short range it averages 210 and penetrates every AV10-14 row and personal armour outright, and the DR 1350 glacis 99% of the time (the meltagun: 87%); beyond ½D the extra die keeps it ahead of the meltagun against AV12-13 (85% and 40%, versus 56% and 10%) while still tailing off to 3% at AV14, matching the fiction's \"bigger meltagun\" framing rather than a full return to short-range lethality. Handling: 55 lb loaded (excluding the 20 lb Heavy Weapon Tripod), ST 14M (mounted, like the other tripod- and vehicle-mounted weapons in heavy.yaml: the sqrt(10x55)=23 a shoulder-fired weapon this heavy would need is carried by the mount) and Gunner (Beams) reflect a support weapon fired from a tripod or vehicle mount; RoF 1 is unchanged, per the family-wide melta vent/recharge rule. Bulk -6 and Rcl 1 are unchanged.",
